---
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import { fenixRunner } from '../../../data/fenixRunner';
import { origin } from '../../../data/site';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { canonicalUrl } from '../../../lib/seo';
import '../../../styles/product.css';

const { legal, unlock } = fenixRunner;
---
<Layout
  title="Fenix Runner — Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using and buying Fenix Runner watch faces: trial, one-time unlock, refunds and liability."
  canonical={canonicalUrl('/FenixRunner/terms')}
  ogImage={`${origin}/fenix-runner-icon.png`}
  preloadHero={false}
>
  <Header slot="header" />
  <article class="product legal">
    <h1>Fenix Runner — Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective <time datetime={legal.effectiveDate}>{legal.effectiveLabel}</time></p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Who and what</h2>
      <p>
        Fenix Runner is a watch face made by Aníbal Ribeiro, Prague, Czech
        Republic ("I", "me"). These terms apply when you install or buy Fenix
        Runner for a Garmin (Connect IQ) watch, or an Amazfit (Zepp OS) watch where offered, and when you
        use the unlock page on this website. If you buy from the Garmin Connect IQ
        Store, Garmin's store terms also apply to that purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Licence</h2>
      <p>
        I grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use
        Fenix Runner on watches you own. You may not copy, resell or redistribute
        it, reverse engineer it except where the law allows, remove the licence
        checks, or share or sell unlock codes. The software, artwork and layouts
        remain mine; bundled fonts stay under their own open licences.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Trial and unlock</h2>
      <p>
        The trial and unlock versions work fully for a trial period, then lock
        until you unlock them. The Garmin trial lasts 48 hours; any other length is stated in
        the store listing. Unlocking costs {unlock.price} USD, paid once, with no
        subscription.
      </p>
      <p>
        An unlock is tied to one watch through its Device Code. It stays valid
        for that watch for the life of the app, including after a reinstall, and
        works without contacting my server. A different watch needs its own
        unlock. A price shown at checkout may include tax or differ by currency.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payments are handled by
        <a href="https://www.creem.io" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creem</a>, which is the
        merchant of record: it sells to you, collects taxes and issues receipts,
        and its terms apply to the payment. I do not receive your card details.
        Purchases from the Garmin Connect IQ Store are charged by Garmin.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        If Fenix Runner does not work for you, email me within 14 days of buying
        and I will refund you through Creem. Include your Device Code or order
        number. A refunded purchase should no longer be used. Purchases from the
        Garmin Connect IQ Store follow Garmin's refund rules instead. Your
        statutory consumer rights are not affected.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Compatibility and changes</h2>
      <p>
        Watch models, firmware and phone apps differ, and data such as heart
        rate or weather depends on what your watch provides. I test on selected
        devices and cannot promise it will look or run the same on every watch.
        I may update, change or stop supporting Fenix Runner. An unlock you have
        paid for is not removed by an update.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. No medical use</h2>
      <p>
        Fenix Runner only displays readings from your watch. It is not a medical
        device and must not be relied on for health or safety decisions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Garmin, Connect IQ, Amazfit, Zepp and other names are trademarks of their
        owners. Fenix Runner is independent and not affiliated with, endorsed by
        or sponsored by them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Warranty and liability</h2>
      <p>
        Fenix Runner is provided "as is", without promises beyond those the law
        requires. To the extent the law allows, I am not liable for indirect or
        lost-profit losses, and my total liability for any claim is limited to
        the amount you paid for the app. Nothing here limits liability that
        cannot be limited by law, including for intent or gross negligence, or
        your mandatory consumer rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        How data is handled is described in the
        <a href="/FenixRunner/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of the Czech Republic. If you are a
        consumer, you keep the protection of the mandatory rules of the country
        where you live. Please contact me first; most problems are solved by
        email. Consumers in the EU may also use the Czech Trade Inspection
        Authority (<a href="https://www.coi.cz" rel="noopener noreferrer">ČOI</a>) for
        out-of-court dispute resolution.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        I may update these terms; changes apply to later purchases and appear
        here with a new effective date. Questions:
        <a href={fenixRunner.supportUrl}>email@anibalribeiro.cz</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <p class="product-links">
    <a href="/FenixRunner/">About Fenix Runner</a>
    <a href="/FenixRunner/privacy/">Privacy</a>
  </p>
  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>
